A||||3||overlord||headlight weirdness..||||1||
Z||000000||overlord||06-10-2000||06:25 PM||||i just bought a pair of hi-output halagen headlights.and now something weird is happening.<P>whenever i start up the car the left headlight works but is very dim, and after 19-20 secs it will come on full power. It does it in low and hi-beam, but only does it when i first start the car up.   Is it a faulty headlight?, since it started doing it after i put in these light.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bill Osmer||06-10-2000||07:44 PM||||Check your connector (at the back ofthe new headlight) - I've had similar experiences, and it's nothing more than a bad/poor connection. To check it, just raise your hood, turn on your lights, then wiggle the connector on the headlight. If it shows varying amounts of broightness and then stays bright, it's definately the connector. If not, it's somehting else and you'll have to continue troubleshooting.||||reg||14
Z||000002||sdm1964||06-11-2000||07:11 AM||||could be the isolation relay going bad. It is the one on the firewall next to the drivers side headlight. Mine went bad and the headlights would come on low and stay on. Had to go to off, then parking lights and then off to get them off. Just my 2 cents||||reg||14
Z||000003||batboy||06-11-2000||08:16 AM||||About 99% of the time if a headlight is dim it's a grounding problem, usually a dirty or loose coonect at the headlight terminal. These sealed beam headlight bulbs have three wires at the plug-in connection. One is a ground and the other two are power leads for the low beam and the high beam. Make sure the terminal contacts are clean and tight. That usually solves the problem in most cases.||||reg||1
